# Hermetic llama-server.log slice for the measured abandoned-prefill window
# model (LP-0MVW8S74G004MFAQ). Covers the same fake window as
# abandoned_prefill_windows_measured_proxy.log; lines carry no wall-clock
# timestamp (real llama-server behaviour), so the analyser is only valid when
# this file covers exactly the analysed window.
#
# Real line shapes copied from /var/log/llama-proxy/llama-server.log*:
#   [pid] slot launch_slot_: id  S | task -1 | sampler chain: ...
#   [pid] slot launch_slot_: id  S | task T | processing task, is_child = 0
#   [pid] slot update_slots: id  S | task T | prompt processing progress, n_tokens = N, batch.n_tokens = B, progress = P
#   [pid] srv          stop: cancel task, id_task = T
#   [pid] prompt eval time =   <ms> ms / <tokens> tokens ( ... )
#   [pid] slot      release: id  S | task T | stop processing: n_tokens = N, truncated = 0
#
# Ground truth (one segment per release, in release order):
#   Segment W1 -> task 51 (release user-one 00:00:00): launch -> 2 progress ->
#       CANCEL -> 2 progress (n_tokens 40000 -> 50000, so 10000 tokens after the
#       cancel) -> prompt eval time (625 tok/s) -> stop processing. Measured
#       cancel->stop = 10000 / 625 = 16.0 s: the window is [00:00:00, 00:00:16].
#   Segment W4 -> task 52 (release user-one 00:02:05): launch -> 2 progress.
#       NO cancel, NO stop processing: unbounded (legacy estimate only).
#   Segment W3 -> task 53 (release user-one 00:02:30): launch -> 2 progress.
#       NO cancel, NO stop processing: unbounded.
#   Segment W2 -> task 54 (release user-two 00:05:00): launch -> 2 progress.
#       NO cancel, NO stop processing: unbounded.
# The needs_measurement discriminator: only task 51 has a cancel + stop pair, so
# only W1 is bounded=basis measured_stop; a naive all-unbounded or all-bounded
# model cannot pass the tests in test_abandoned_prefill_windows_measured.py.
